      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": false,
        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "Compounds 1–4 were prepared similarly. PhSi(OMe)3 (8.0 mmol) and NaOH (8.0 mmol) were dissolved in 30 mL ethanol and heated at reflux for 1.0 h. Then Ln(NO3)3·6H2O (4.0 mmol) and Et4NCl (for 1 and 3) or Ph4PCl (for 2 and 4) (4.0 mmol) in 30 mL CH3CN were added at once and the mixture was heated at reflux for 3 h. Filtration gave a colorless solution; slow evaporation of ethanol/CH3CN over 5–10 days afforded crystals, which were vacuum-dried for analysis and yield. For 1, reactants were PhSi(OMe)3 (0.489 g, 2.5 mmol), NaOH (0.0988 g, 2.5 mmol), Eu(NO3)3·6H2O (0.550 g, 1.23 mmol), and Et4NCl (0.203 g, 1.23 mmol).",
